. * F4. Identify the small-sample convention of the Python clustered SE.
. *     se_cr0 is the plain cluster sandwich computed in Mata (no small-sample factor).
. *     Candidates = (cluster factor) x (observations factor). Nothing here is tuned: all 15
. *     candidates are listed and the one that reproduces the Python SE for the SA coefficient of the main model
. *     coefficient is then used for every other coefficient.
. gen double Ks   = k

. gen double Kyr  = k + (Ny - 1)

. gen double Kall = k + (Ny - 1) + G24

. forvalues gi = 0/2 {
  2.     forvalues ni = 0/4 {
  3.         quietly gen double fg = 1
  4.         if `gi' == 1 quietly replace fg = G22 / (G22 - 1)
  5.         if `gi' == 2 quietly replace fg = G24 / (G24 - 1)
  6.         quietly gen double fn = 1
  7.         if `ni' == 1 quietly replace fn = (N - 1) / (N - Ks)
  8.         if `ni' == 2 quietly replace fn = (N - 1) / (N - Kyr)
  9.         if `ni' == 3 quietly replace fn = (N - 1) / (N - Kall)
 10.         if `ni' == 4 quietly replace fn = N / (N - Kall)
 11.         quietly gen double cs_`gi'_`ni' = se_cr0 * sqrt(fg * fn)
 12.         quietly gen double er_`gi'_`ni' = abs(cs_`gi'_`ni' / py_se_cr1 - 1)
 13.         drop fg fn
 14.     }
 15. }

